    "title": "Video Of Peyton Manning's Son Throwing Pass Has 1.5 Million Views",
    "text": "Wow.Mar 15, 2026 4:01 PM EDTMarshall Manning throwing pass. CBS Sports.Key PointsMarshall Manning, Peyton's 14-year-old son, gains attention as a football recruit.His passing video at a 7-on-7 event reached 1.5 million views online.Ohio State, Georgia, and Tennessee are early contenders for Marshall's college choice. The apple doesn’t fall far from the tree in the Manning family. While Archie, Peyton and Eli Manning all starred in the National Football League, Arch Manning is currently a top NFL Draft prospect at the University of Texas. And there’s another Manning coming. Marshall Manning, the 14-year-old son of Peyton Manning, is already emerging in recruiting circles. Over the weekend, he was seen throwing at a 7-on-7 event. Video of Marshall Manning completing a pass down the right sideline already has 1.5 million views. “Like father, like son! ☝️,” CBS Sports wrote on Instagram. (You can see the video here). Marshall Manning is a Class of 2030 recruit out of The Baylor School. It’s early, but three schools have been named contenders Three schools – Ohio State, Georgia and Tennessee – have been named contenders for Marshall Manning’s services. Tennessee, the hometown option, might be the favorite. The Vols were once led by Peyton Manning and could soon be led by his son. Where do you see him ending up? This page may contain affiliate links to legal sports betting or fantasy sports partners. If you sign up, The Spun and The Arena Group may be compensated at no cost to you. Read more about Sports Betting on The Spun.About the authorAndrew Holleran has been leading coverage at The Spun since 2014, with 15 years of experience covering college football, the NFL, sports media and more.",
